{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition","id":977918,"title":"Has Everyone Gone to New Eddition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T13:01:39-07:00","id":977918,"title":"Has Everyone Gone to New Eddition?","content":"Hello. I just really want to know this. I've been getting nWoD (I think of nWoD to be the &quot;first&quot; edition. Vampire the Requiem to Mummy the Curse. Chronicles is Demons and updated versions) for at least five or six years. And I have a decent collection scattered between the lines. And I would actually like to try out the games someday. But I've never had a group to try them with. And it seems like all the online games are with Chronicles. So I have a hard time making futile attempts to play that way.<br /> <br /> I don't really want to switch. I know that nWoD had some real stupid problems. But I don't like change and like collecting the books. So I don't want to move to Chronicles. A lot of what I've heard about Chronicles is cool, but some of it annoys me. The whole werewolves on 100% diets. The beat system and the Fatelike conditions. The changes of Changeling Seemings to be based on how you escape arcadia.<br /> <br /> I know there are cool things. Like the Huntsmen in Changeling, Demon is cool. And probably the factions are realized in a less stupid way. But I don't really like change.<br /> <br /> So, does anyone still play without the GMC changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:14:00-07:00","id":977930,"title":"","content":"I don't but I know there are people who do, they post about it all the time. And obviously fans of Mummy still just play first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:43:28-07:00","id":977945,"title":"","content":"Every 2e update so far has been a flat-out improvement over 1e. You'd have to be real persuasive to make me go back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:43:50-07:00","id":977946,"title":"","content":"I know of a few posters here who stick to first edition. They're in the minority, but they're out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:45:17-07:00","id":977947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=977945#post977945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every 2e update so far has been a flat-out improvement over 1e. You'd have to be real persuasive to make me go back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, especially since it's so easy to adapt 1e material to 2e if you do desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:13:14-07:00","id":978019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=977947#post977947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed, especially since it's so easy to adapt 1e material to 2e if you do desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>not for everyone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:43:07-07:00","id":978041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978019#post978019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not for everyone...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of it you don't even have to do anything to convert. Just add Athetics to any pre-written characters' Defense, and swap out bonus dice from weapons for bonus damage. Most Merits can be ported directly, unless they allow for multiple attacks and those you can just replace with a &quot;close enough&quot; equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:49:41-07:00","id":978046,"title":"","content":"Second edition is head and shoulders above the first. It's particularly true in the earliest games. But a decade of time and the real world context of how those early books were devised probably has something to do with it. I'm excited about all the 2E books, and I'm sure they'll all benefit from having player experience and perspective to draw from, but god, 2E Requiem in particular was just so strong. I don't expect that much discrepancy in a lot of the later books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:36:11-07:00","id":978064,"title":"","content":"I don't like change must either when it comes to my RPGs, it was a year + before I even gave Vampire: the Requiem a glance at my local FLGS. I had dozens of cWoD books and zero interest in changing over. Then I was bored one day and in a Barns &amp; Nobles and gave V:tR a read and found I loved it. I bought it that night and spent hours reading it the next few nights and later at my FLGS checked out the other lines and rapidly switched over. I felt like I lost out somewhat in being so abstinent about nWoD.<br /> <br /> So I know exactly where you are coming from and when 2e was announced I looked at my collection and the hundreds I'd spent over the years and groaned. Thank the gods that Onyx Path - in their awesomeness - decided to do open development and poured over material released and loved every aspect of it. Now not everyone does, but as others have said each of the 2nd ed/Chronicles have been head and shoulders better than the 1e books, taking fan ideas and taking into accounts mistakes and issues of the 1e books and simply creating fantastic new lines.<br /> <br /> Not everyone likes every aspect of Chronicles, while they may be the minority - not liking as you state: the beast system, or conditions; that doesn't mean your opinion is invalid. Thankfully these systems aren't integral and you can play CofD without them. Also a great deal of material from the 1st edition can be easily updated to CofD - as others have said - sans perhaps the combat merits. So you won't need to throw out a lot of the books you bought. Even better, each line has all the rules in the core book, no longer needing the base 'World of Darkness' for the rules. So want to check out Werewolf: the Forsaken (Perhaps the most improved of the released 2e lines), you don't need to buy two books. Hell, just buy the $15 PDF, it's all you really need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:40:18-07:00","id":978069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978064#post978064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like change must either when it comes to my RPGs, it was a year + before I even gave Vampire: the Requiem a glance at my local FLGS. I had dozens of cWoD books and zero interest in changing over. Then I was bored one day and in a Barns &amp; Nobles and gave V:tR a read and found I loved it. I bought it that night and spent hours reading it the next few nights and later at my FLGS checked out the other lines and rapidly switched over. I felt like I lost out somewhat in being so abstinent about nWoD.<br /> <br /> So I know exactly where you are coming from and when 2e was announced I looked at my collection and the hundreds I'd spent over the years and groaned. Thank the gods that Onyx Path - in their awesomeness - decided to do open development and poured over material released and loved every aspect of it. Now not everyone does, but as others have said each of the 2nd ed/Chronicles have been head and shoulders better than the 1e books, taking fan ideas and taking into accounts mistakes and issues of the 1e books and simply creating fantastic new lines.<br /> <br /> Not everyone likes every aspect of Chronicles, while they may be the minority - not liking as you state: the beast system, or conditions; that doesn't mean your opinion is invalid. Thankfully these systems aren't integral and you can play CofD without them. Also a great deal of material from the 1st edition can be easily updated to CofD - as others have said - sans perhaps the combat merits. So you won't need to throw out a lot of the books you bought. Even better, each line has all the rules in the core book, no longer needing the base 'World of Darkness' for the rules. So want to check out Werewolf: the Forsaken (Perhaps the most improved of the released 2e lines), you don't need to buy two books. Hell, just buy the $15 PDF, it's all you really need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best answer in the thread right here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:03:12-07:00","id":978087,"title":"","content":"The Beat system is a simple idea that proves surprisingly difficult to articulate. Streamlining the math involved in character advancement is great, but it adds an extra step in the traditional &quot;do thing, get XP, buy shit&quot; formula that most RPGers have internalized for decades. I've found it easiest to just call Beats XP and multiply all the Experience costs by five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:09:04-07:00","id":978089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978087#post978087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beat system is a simple idea that proves surprisingly difficult to articulate. Streamlining the math involved in character advancement is great, but it adds an extra step in the traditional &amp;quot;do thing, get XP, buy shit&amp;quot; formula that most RPGers have internalized for decades. I've found it easiest to just call Beats XP and multiply all the Experience costs by five.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a combination of this, and the &quot;director stance&quot; nature of many of the ways Beats are acquired that puts a lot of folks off of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:14:28-07:00","id":978096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978089#post978089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's a combination of this, and the &quot;director stance&quot; nature of many of the ways Beats are acquired that puts a lot of folks off of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, its meant to encourage role-play and dramatic moments but it can also be seen as making people jump through hoops. It more directly links character advancement to specific experiences rather than just soaking up ambient points from the air, but can also come off like its holding advancement hostage unless you perform correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:40:44-07:00","id":978112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978096#post978096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, its meant to encourage role-play and dramatic moments but it can also be seen as making people jump through hoops. It more directly links character advancement to specific experiences rather than just soaking up ambient points from the air, but can also come off like its holding advancement hostage unless you perform correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to the fact that it requires the player to make decisions based on factors that are beyond the character's frame of reference. The classic example being the Spooked Condition, which does nothing on its own and only grants a Beat when the character does something that hinders the group. There are some folks who prefer the players desires and the characters desires to always be in-sync, to make decisions for their characters based exclusively on the characters' motivations and perspectives. I, personally, don't agree with that perspective, but it's a pretty common one in the hobby, and I think what people are usually trying to express when they say things like &quot;I don't like storygame mechanics&quot; or &quot;Conditions are too much like FATE.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:43:03-07:00","id":978195,"title":"","content":"Mhhm. I do agree that it is better. Definitely a big part of my aversion is the whole time investment. Just, if I decide to invest energy into Chronicles Edition I will have a lot of books to read and a lot of time that will feel wasted. Just, I've invested a lot of energy in the (some nickname for edition referring to previous moniker) and just going over the same ground again would be in some ways disappointing. Now I'm in a poor mood which complicates this communication.<br /> <br /> But, also oddly I actually kind of like Fate. I haven't looked at a lot of it. But I read and enjoyed the Dresden Files RPG core. I'm not certain what the difference is, And I'll admit I haven't looked to closely at the Chronicles rule-set. I think it has something to do with how I think about the games. Where I would want to use FATE for playing just a certain type of game. Just, not kick in the door or straight action. More like relating to the character as someone in a story than going for a more direct connection. I don't know,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:08:20-07:00","id":978206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978195#post978195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhhm. I do agree that it is better. Definitely a big part of my aversion is the whole time investment. Just, if I decide to invest energy into Chronicles Edition I will have a lot of books to read and a lot of time that will feel wasted. Just, I've invested a lot of energy in the (some nickname for edition referring to previous moniker) and just going over the same ground again would be in some ways disappointing. Now I'm in a poor mood which complicates this communication.<br /> <br /> But, also oddly I actually kind of like Fate. I haven't looked at a lot of it. But I read and enjoyed the Dresden Files RPG core. I'm not certain what the difference is, And I'll admit I haven't looked to closely at the Chronicles rule-set. I think it has something to do with how I think about the games. Where I would want to use FATE for playing just a certain type of game. Just, not kick in the door or straight action. More like relating to the character as someone in a story than going for a more direct connection. I don't know,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The core rules really aren't that different. Combat is a bit more vicious (all armed attacks do lethal damage now, and weapon damage is calculated as a flat number rather than an addition to the dice pool), and morality has been replaced with a more flexible integrity system. The most complicated change is the new experience system which, as said, is very much like the FATE system. It's a cool little rules set that rewards players for dramatic moments, even (or especially) if those moments are failures for their characters.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a game, and the only ones out there are 2E, I say make the plunge. It's a game worth playing, and it shouldn't take much investment in time or money. God Machine Chronicles covers the basic changes, and I think you'd get along just fine with one of the 1E books and that. If I remember correctly, the PDF is free online, and the conversion rules are only about 50-60 pages long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:17:21-07:00","id":978210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978195#post978195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mhhm. I do agree that it is better. Definitely a big part of my aversion is the whole time investment. Just, if I decide to invest energy into Chronicles Edition I will have a lot of books to read and a lot of time that will feel wasted. Just, I've invested a lot of energy in the (some nickname for edition referring to previous moniker) and just going over the same ground again would be in some ways disappointing. Now I'm in a poor mood which complicates this communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>The time and energy you've invested into 1st edition isn't wasted if you adopt the 2nd edition rules changes. The settings are still largely the same, with some changes you are free to use or ignore as you see fit, but ultimately most of what you know from 1e still holds true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978195#post978195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, also oddly I actually kind of like Fate. I haven't looked at a lot of it. But I read and enjoyed the Dresden Files RPG core. I'm not certain what the difference is, And I'll admit I haven't looked to closely at the Chronicles rule-set.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would highly recommend looking closely at it. It keeps most of the core mechanics pretty much the same, but improves greatly on a lot of details in the various subsystems. Don't knock it 'till you've tried it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978195#post978195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it has something to do with how I think about the games. Where I would want to use FATE for playing just a certain type of game. Just, not kick in the door or straight action. More like relating to the character as someone in a story than going for a more direct connection. I don't know,</div> </div> </div> </div>The <s>New World</s> Chronicles of Darkness has always aimed for relating to the characters as someone in a story. It's even called the Storytelling system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:23:50-07:00","id":978252,"title":"","content":"Once Mummy moves to 2e I plan to dive into it but haven't made the transition fully<br /> yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-29-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:49:21-07:00","id":978261,"title":"","content":"Saying from guy that run two chronicles on GMC, not finished rules - new Beats &amp; Condition system is all you will take of it. You can totally play games without them - just treat Condition mentions as 'rule X on page YY' in 1E gamebooks. My older <b>Mage</b> group almost not using those. Second, younger one, use them from time to time. Still, Beats system seems more 'fair' to me - you get XP for making game more interesting/risking and playing your <i>character</i>, not on how much ST had mood to give you or how you as die-hard RP player would take on it. I even make group XP splitting after sessions, where all players can say if particular character really fulfilled her traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T03:46:02-07:00","id":978300,"title":"","content":"not enough ppl moved to 2nd ed, imo :P I just can't play 1ed... After tying it thought bout playing mummy, then I realized it's still in first. Postponed it until it get's a second edition update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:48:32-07:00","id":978351,"title":"","content":"Personally, i will be sticking to 1st edition for changeling none of the changes from 2nd editions changeling are so far anything that interest me.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, in PBP Chrod is not feasible to apply as many of the rules dont work in the context of a multithread PBP so i apply a mixture of 1st and 2nd.<br /> <br /> 2nd editions merits, combat and linear XP, but 1st lack of beats, conditions and tilts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:12:53-07:00","id":978368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978351#post978351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, i will be sticking to 1st edition for changeling none of the changes from 2nd editions changeling are so far anything that interest me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the rules updates are worth it alone, the core system of CoD is better across the board, imo. We haven't really seen much for Changeling, however. Who know's how the substantive body of work will turn out. Judging by the rest of the 2e books however I'd give it a shot. I loved CtL but it certainly had it's problems. Hopefully they'll be able to smooth that out. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7892-malraza","name":"Malraza","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:02:42-07:00","id":978487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malraza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978368#post978368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the rules updates are worth it alone, the core system of CoD is better across the board, imo. We haven't really seen much for Changeling, however. Who know's how the substantive body of work will turn out. Judging by the rest of the 2e books however I'd give it a shot. I loved CtL but it certainly had it's problems. Hopefully they'll be able to smooth that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally the only problem i had with Changeling how unecesary dreams were. So form me the new things are just uncesary add ons. Huntmen, superforms, dreams, courts, narrative focus are things not for my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:20:38-07:00","id":978568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978210#post978210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <s>New World</s> Chronicles of Darkness has always aimed for relating to the characters as someone in a story. It's even called the Storytelling system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think saying FATE is for stories is not what I quite meant. More like, FATE is more like, CBS. A lot of their programming imo comes down to being an adventure. Not like a D&amp;D adventure with a dungeon crawl or something. But much of the time it is about the main characters facing a problem in their bailiwick. While Chronicles of Darkness and New World of Darkness are a bit more like HBO drama. Without as much of the gratuitous fan service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:03:06-07:00","id":978852,"title":"","content":"So far I like the 2nd ed for all the games minus CtL. I really dislike how they switched Kiths and Seemings and redid the Courts. But those are easily kept the same and just upgrade the mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:14:33-07:00","id":978857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/977918-has-everyone-gone-to-new-eddition?p=978568#post978568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without as much of the gratuitous fan service.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the way I do it. And I've tried, but come on, why limit yourself.<br /> <br /> This seems more of a matter of perception than how the game is put out there. Which is fair, if that's how you've experienced it, but all you would have to do is run a game a little differently to change it about. The rules and system aren't determining how the story is told, they're there to give the players tools to work within the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}